ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I definitely think it makes sense to have `VariantType` be accessed outside `Variant`. \r\nThe way I interpret it, variant types are really owned by Godot (not `Variant`), and `Variant` is just a single-value collection type using it. `TypedArray` is another similar type (which 'happens' to use `Variant` to store its values because it's built on `Array`).\r\n\r\nOperators should probably not be owned by `Variant` in the first place. It seem to me better suited for some kind of variant functions database (which doesn't exist). But I don't mind having them here for now.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101995#pullrequestreview-2724966121","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101995","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101995#pullrequestreview-2724966121"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101995"}},"submitted_at":"2025-03-28T10:09:13Z","commit_id":null}]